  "notes": [
    "S5-HVS1 (Gaia DR2 6513109241989477504) is the only included star: the paper explicitly calls it unbound based on its radial velocity alone (T:p3-b2) and retains the hyper-velocity (unbound) classification in the conclusions (T:p14-b11). Other HVS discussed for comparison (T:p9-b3) are not individually established as Galactic unbound candidates in this paper; J01020100 is described there as a bound disk runaway.",
    "S5-HVS1: No numerical bound/unbound probability or galactocentric radius is reported for S5-HVS1. Distances are also reported in the paper in logarithmic form (log10 Dhel/1 kpc); those values duplicate the listed m-M distances and are not separately retained. At T:p9-b7 the predicted μα cos δ is given as 35.333 ± 0.081 mas/yr, whereas Table 1 and T:p14-b7 give ±0.080 mas/yr; I retain ±0.080 and treat the former as a likely typo. The Section 4 text at T:p7-b3 quotes Model P V3D,now = 1470^{+166}_{-147} km/s, while T:p7-b7 quotes 1470^{+170}_{-150} km/s; both are reported, and I retain the latter final posterior summary while noting the discrepancy. The predicted distance corresponding to ϖ = 0.11 mas is printed at T:p14-b7 as 8 828 kpc with a missing decimal; I do not retain it as a separate distance because it is a prediction and the formatting is ambiguous."
  ]
